@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-senior-inspector`

-- g5-tests-senior-inspector.l4: tests of g5-senior-inspector.l4 (ss.33 and 34).
-- Expected values were decided from the Hebrew of ss.33 and 34 (inputs/law.wiki lines 269 to 287, and s.29(a),
-- lines 229 to 238, which s.33 def.3 carries over) BEFORE any of this was run.  A DEONTIC cannot be compared in
-- #ASSERT, so the rules are exercised with #TRACE, each with its expected result written above it as
-- `-- EXPECT:` and checked by work/g5/tracecheck.py.

§ `Tests of ss 33 and 34`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- Person: an employee of a testing body, engaged to be relied on, authorised to test, authorised to give opinions
--                                                              employee  engaged  tests  opinions
`an employee authorised only to test`           MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE
`an employee authorised only to give opinions`  MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`an employee authorised for both`               MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE
`an engaged person authorised only to test`     MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE,  FALSE
`an engaged person authorised to give opinions` MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, TRUE
`an engaged person with no authorisation`       MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF FALSE, TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE
`an employee with no authorisation`             MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF TRUE,  FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a stranger who holds both authorisations`      MEANS `Person who may be a tester or an expert` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE,  TRUE

-- List: set by the senior inspector, set for the carrying out of an auxiliary test
`a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test` MEANS `List used in a test under section 33` OF TRUE,  TRUE
`a list set by someone else`                                MEANS `List used in a test under section 33` OF FALSE, TRUE
`a list set for no auxiliary test`                          MEANS `List used in a test under section 33` OF TRUE,  FALSE

-- Test: performed by, at the senior inspector's requirement, on the basis of a list, the list
--                                                                     performer                                     requirement  basis  list
`a test by a tester`                      MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an employee authorised only to test`,           TRUE,  TRUE,  `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
`a test by an engaged expert`             MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an engaged person authorised to give opinions`, TRUE,  TRUE,  `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
`a test by an engaged tester-only`        MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an engaged person authorised only to test`,     TRUE,  TRUE,  `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
`a test by someone with no authorisation` MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an employee with no authorisation`,             TRUE,  TRUE,  `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
`a test not at the senior inspector's requirement` MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an employee authorised only to test`,  FALSE, TRUE,  `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
`a test on no list`                       MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an employee authorised only to test`,           TRUE,  FALSE, `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
`a test on a list nobody set as a checklist` MEANS `Test under section 33` OF `an employee authorised only to test`,        TRUE,  TRUE,  `a list set by someone else`

§§ `s 33 -- Definitions`

-- def.2 (src:272): tester = an employee of a testing body authorised under s.36 to carry out auxiliary tests.
#ASSERT `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` `an employee authorised only to test`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` `an employee authorised for both`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` `an employee authorised only to give opinions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` `an engaged person authorised only to test`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` `an employee with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 2 — the person is a tester` `a stranger who holds both authorisations`

-- def.5 (src:275): expert = an employee or a person engaged, authorised to test or to give opinions.  Read
-- literally it takes in an employee authorised only to test (fork F-OVERLAP), so the first assertion below is
-- the overlap; the alternative reading removes it and keeps the rest.
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised only to test`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised only to give opinions`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised for both`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an engaged person authorised only to test`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an engaged person authorised to give opinions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an engaged person with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an employee with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `a stranger who holds both authorisations`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised only to test`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised only to give opinions`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised for both`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an engaged person authorised only to test`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an engaged person authorised to give opinions`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an engaged person with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 5, an employee authorised only to test being a tester and not an expert — the person is an expert` `an employee with no authorisation`
-- s.34(c), last words, as an avoidance-of-doubt test: an expert employed by a testing body remains possible.
#ASSERT `s 33 def 5 — the person is an expert` `an employee authorised for both`
-- def.1 and def.7 (src:271, 277).
#ASSERT `s 33 def 7 — the list is a checklist` `a list set by the senior inspector for an auxiliary test`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 7 — the list is a checklist` `a list set by someone else`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 7 — the list is a checklist` `a list set for no auxiliary test`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test by a tester`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test by an engaged expert`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test by an engaged tester-only`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test by someone with no authorisation`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test not at the senior inspector's requirement`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test on no list`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 1 — the test is an auxiliary test` `a test on a list nobody set as a checklist`

-- def.4 (src:274): a testing body meets s.35 and was engaged to be relied on.
#ASSERT `s 33 def 4 — the corporation is a testing body` (`Corporation under section 33` OF TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 4 — the corporation is a testing body` (`Corporation under section 33` OF TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 4 — the corporation is a testing body` (`Corporation under section 33` OF FALSE, TRUE)

-- def.3 (src:273; s.29(a), src:230, 234-238): the sixteen listed relationships are all family members; a step
-- relationship is included, and a person with no listed relationship is not one however he is otherwise connected.
`every family relationship in the list` MEANS
    LIST `the spouse of the subject`, `a parent of the subject`, `a parent of a parent of the subject`, `a son or daughter of the subject`, `the spouse of a son or daughter of the subject`, `a brother or sister of the subject`,
         `a child of a brother or sister of the subject`, `a brother-in-law of the subject`, `a sister-in-law of the subject`, `an uncle or aunt of the subject`, `a child of an uncle or aunt of the subject`,
         `the subject's wife's father`, `the subject's wife's mother`, `the subject's husband's father`, `the subject's husband's mother`, `a grandchild of the subject`

#ASSERT count `every family relationship in the list` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT all (GIVEN relationship YIELD `s 33 def 3 — the person is a family member of the subject` (`How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF (JUST relationship), FALSE)) `every family relationship in the list`
#ASSERT all (GIVEN relationship YIELD `s 33 def 3 — the person is a family member of the subject` (`How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF (JUST relationship), TRUE)) `every family relationship in the list`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a family member of the subject` (`How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF NOTHING, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a family member of the subject` (`How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF NOTHING, TRUE)

-- "Relative", limbs (1) to (4): each alone is enough; none is not.
`a brother` MEANS `How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF (JUST `a brother or sister of the subject`), FALSE
`nobody in particular` MEANS `How a person is related to the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF NOTHING, FALSE
--                                                                           how related       economic  corporation  body
`a relative by limb 1`  MEANS `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF `a brother`,           FALSE,    FALSE,       FALSE
`a relative by limb 2`  MEANS `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF `nobody in particular`, TRUE,     FALSE,       FALSE
`a relative by limb 3`  MEANS `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF `nobody in particular`, FALSE,    TRUE,        FALSE
`a relative by limb 4`  MEANS `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF `nobody in particular`, FALSE,    FALSE,       TRUE
`a stranger`            MEANS `Person who may be a relative of the subject (s 33 def 3)` OF `nobody in particular`, FALSE,    FALSE,       FALSE
#ASSERT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` `a relative by limb 1`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` `a relative by limb 2`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` `a relative by limb 3`
#ASSERT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` `a relative by limb 4`
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 3 — the person is a relative of the subject` `a stranger`

-- def.6 (src:276): conflict of interest, the subject's own or a relative's.
`an interest of the subject's brother that conflicts`      MEANS `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` OF `a relative by limb 1`, TRUE
`an interest of the subject's brother that does not conflict` MEANS `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` OF `a relative by limb 1`, FALSE
`an interest of a dependant that conflicts`               MEANS `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` OF `a relative by limb 2`, TRUE
`an interest of a corporation that conflicts`             MEANS `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` OF `a relative by limb 3`, TRUE
`an interest of a body that conflicts`                    MEANS `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` OF `a relative by limb 4`, TRUE
`an interest of a stranger that conflicts`                MEANS `Other person with an interest or role (s 33 def 6)` OF `a stranger`, TRUE
--                                                        own conflict  others
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF TRUE, EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, EMPTY)
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of the subject's brother that conflicts`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of the subject's brother that does not conflict`)
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of a dependant that conflicts`)
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of a corporation that conflicts`)
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of a body that conflicts`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of a stranger that conflicts`)
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF FALSE, LIST `an interest of a stranger that conflicts`, `an interest of the subject's brother that conflicts`)
#ASSERT `s 33 def 6 — the subject is in a conflict of interest` (`Situation of a possible conflict of interest of a tester, expert or testing body` OF TRUE, LIST `an interest of a stranger that conflicts`)

§§ `s 34(a) -- the senior inspector`

`an inspector` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as the senior inspector` OF TRUE
`someone who is not an inspector` MEANS `Candidate for authorisation as the senior inspector` OF FALSE
`the senior inspector authorised from among the inspectors` MEANS `authorise an inspector as the senior inspector` `an inspector`
`the senior inspector authorised from outside the inspectors` MEANS `authorise an inspector as the senior inspector` `someone who is not an inspector`

-- s.34(a) (src:280): duty reading (taken).  Authorising an inspector discharges it; authorising a non-inspector does
-- not; with no time stated, waiting leaves it standing.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(a) — the Minister shall authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the senior inspector authorised from among the inspectors` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(a) — the Minister shall authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the senior inspector authorised from outside the inspectors` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(a) — the Minister shall authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- Fork F-DUTY: read as a power, the same act is FULFILLED.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the senior inspector authorised from among the inspectors` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(a), read as a power — the Minister may authorise a senior inspector from among the inspectors` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `the senior inspector authorised from outside the inspectors` AT 4

§§ `s 34(b) -- reliance on findings and opinions`

-- Material: kind, the test, the expert who gave the opinion (if an opinion), for supervising the Law
--                                                                    kind                                                        test                          giver                                           supervising
`findings of a tester on a proper test`       MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`,          `a test by a tester`,            NOTHING,                                         TRUE
`findings of an expert on a proper test`      MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by an expert`,         `a test by an engaged expert`,   NOTHING,                                         TRUE
`findings said to be a tester's, by an engaged person` MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`, `a test by an engaged tester-only`, NOTHING,                                       TRUE
`an opinion by an engaged expert on an expert's test` MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `an expert opinion on the results of an auxiliary test`, `a test by an engaged expert`, (JUST `an engaged person authorised to give opinions`), TRUE
`an opinion with no named expert`             MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `an expert opinion on the results of an auxiliary test`, `a test by an engaged expert`, NOTHING,                                       TRUE
`an opinion by someone who is no expert`      MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `an expert opinion on the results of an auxiliary test`, `a test by an engaged expert`, (JUST `an employee with no authorisation`), TRUE
`an opinion on a test by someone who is no expert` MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `an expert opinion on the results of an auxiliary test`, `a test by someone with no authorisation`, (JUST `an engaged person authorised to give opinions`), TRUE
`findings of a tester but not for supervision` MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`,          `a test by a tester`,            NOTHING,                                         FALSE
`findings of a test not at his requirement`   MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`,          `a test not at the senior inspector's requirement`, NOTHING,                  TRUE
`findings of a test by someone with no authorisation` MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by a tester`, `a test by someone with no authorisation`, NOTHING,                           TRUE
`an employee-tester's findings put forward as an expert's` MEANS `Material offered to the senior inspector` OF `findings of an auxiliary test done by an expert`, `a test by a tester`, NOTHING,                                       TRUE

#ASSERT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `findings of a tester on a proper test`
#ASSERT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `findings of an expert on a proper test`
#ASSERT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `an opinion by an engaged expert on an expert's test`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `findings said to be a tester's, by an engaged person`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `an opinion with no named expert`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `an opinion by someone who is no expert`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `an opinion on a test by someone who is no expert`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `findings of a tester but not for supervision`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `findings of a test not at his requirement`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `findings of a test by someone with no authorisation`
-- On the literal def.5 an employee authorised only to test is an expert too, so his findings may be relied on as an expert's.
#ASSERT `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on the material` `an employee-tester's findings put forward as an expert's`
#ASSERT `s 34(b)(2) — the opinion was given by an expert` (JUST `an engaged person authorised to give opinions`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b)(2) — the opinion was given by an expert` (JUST `an employee with no authorisation`)
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(b)(2) — the opinion was given by an expert` NOTHING

`the reliance on a tester's findings` MEANS `rely on material from an auxiliary test` `findings of a tester on a proper test`
`the reliance on an unsupervised tester's findings` MEANS `rely on material from an auxiliary test` `findings of a tester but not for supervision`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on auxiliary test findings and expert opinions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the senior inspector` DOES `the reliance on a tester's findings` AT 3
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(b) — the senior inspector may rely on auxiliary test findings and expert opinions` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the senior inspector` DOES `the reliance on an unsupervised tester's findings` AT 3

§§ `s 34(c) -- engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law`

`an engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law` MEANS `Engagement for reliance under section 34(b)` OF TRUE
`an engagement made without a tender` MEANS `Engagement for reliance under section 34(b)` OF FALSE
#ASSERT `s 34(c) — the engagement is made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` `an engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(c) — the engagement is made in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` `an engagement made without a tender`

`engaging a testing body under a tender` MEANS `engage a testing body or an expert for reliance` `an engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law`
`engaging a testing body without a tender` MEANS `engage a testing body or an expert for reliance` `an engagement made without a tender`
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Ministry`
#TRACE `s 34(c) — the Ministry shall engage a testing body or an expert to be relied on only in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `engaging a testing body without a tender` AT 2
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(c) — the Ministry shall engage a testing body or an expert to be relied on only in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Ministry` DOES `engaging a testing body under a tender` AT 2
-- Fork F-ACTOR: the text names no engaging party; with the Minister as the party the same act is the same breach.
-- EXPECT: BREACH BY `the Minister`
#TRACE `s 34(c) — a testing body or an expert shall be engaged to be relied on only in accordance with the Mandatory Tenders Law, the party engaging being` `the Minister` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `engaging a testing body without a tender` AT 2

§§ `s 34(d) -- the testing body's report`

`a report covering the test, signed by the manager` MEANS `Report by a testing body under section 34(d)` OF TRUE, TRUE
`a report covering the test, not signed by the manager` MEANS `Report by a testing body under section 34(d)` OF TRUE, FALSE
`a signed report that covers no test` MEANS `Report by a testing body under section 34(d)` OF FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34(d) — the report covers the auxiliary test and its findings and is signed by the manager` `a report covering the test, signed by the manager`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(d) — the report covers the auxiliary test and its findings and is signed by the manager` `a report covering the test, not signed by the manager`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(d) — the report covers the auxiliary test and its findings and is signed by the manager` `a signed report that covers no test`

`the testing body's signed report` MEANS `report an auxiliary test and its findings` `a report covering the test, signed by the manager`
`the testing body's unsigned report` MEANS `report an auxiliary test and its findings` `a report covering the test, not signed by the manager`
-- The engaged body that reports as required: FULFILLED.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(d) — an engaged testing body shall report each auxiliary test and its findings to the senior inspector` `an engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `the testing body's signed report` AT 9
-- A report the manager did not sign does not count: the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(d) — an engaged testing body shall report each auxiliary test and its findings to the senior inspector` `an engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a testing body` DOES `the testing body's unsigned report` AT 9
-- No time is stated, so waiting breaches nothing.
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(d) — an engaged testing body shall report each auxiliary test and its findings to the senior inspector` `an engagement under the Mandatory Tenders Law` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- A body engaged otherwise is outside (d): no duty arises.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(d) — an engaged testing body shall report each auxiliary test and its findings to the senior inspector` `an engagement made without a tender` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)

§§ `s 34(e) -- the expert's report and opinion`

`an expert engaged under a tender, not employed` MEANS `Position of an expert under section 34(e)` OF TRUE, FALSE
`an expert employed by a testing body, not himself engaged` MEANS `Position of an expert under section 34(e)` OF FALSE, TRUE
`an expert neither engaged under a tender nor employed` MEANS `Position of an expert under section 34(e)` OF FALSE, FALSE
#ASSERT `s 34(e) — the expert is engaged in accordance with section 34(c) or employed by a testing body` `an expert engaged under a tender, not employed`
#ASSERT `s 34(e) — the expert is engaged in accordance with section 34(c) or employed by a testing body` `an expert employed by a testing body, not himself engaged`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(e) — the expert is engaged in accordance with section 34(c) or employed by a testing body` `an expert neither engaged under a tender nor employed`

-- Report: covers the test, gives his opinion on the results, signed by the expert
`a full report and opinion signed by the expert` MEANS `Report by an expert under section 34(e)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a report with no opinion` MEANS `Report by an expert under section 34(e)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`an unsigned report and opinion` MEANS `Report by an expert under section 34(e)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`an opinion on no test` MEANS `Report by an expert under section 34(e)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
#ASSERT `s 34(e) — the report covers the auxiliary test, gives the opinion on its results and is signed by the expert` `a full report and opinion signed by the expert`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(e) — the report covers the auxiliary test, gives the opinion on its results and is signed by the expert` `a report with no opinion`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(e) — the report covers the auxiliary test, gives the opinion on its results and is signed by the expert` `an unsigned report and opinion`
#ASSERT NOT `s 34(e) — the report covers the auxiliary test, gives the opinion on its results and is signed by the expert` `an opinion on no test`

`the expert's full signed report` MEANS `report an auxiliary test and give an opinion on its results` `a full report and opinion signed by the expert`
`the expert's report without an opinion` MEANS `report an auxiliary test and give an opinion on its results` `a report with no opinion`
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(e) — an engaged or employed expert shall report each auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results` `an expert engaged under a tender, not employed` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `the expert's full signed report` AT 6
-- An employed expert is bound although no engagement of his own was made.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(e) — an engaged or employed expert shall report each auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results` `an expert employed by a testing body, not himself engaged` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `the expert's full signed report` AT 6
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(e) — an engaged or employed expert shall report each auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results` `an expert employed by a testing body, not himself engaged` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `the expert's report without an opinion` AT 6
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(e) — an engaged or employed expert shall report each auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results` `an expert employed by a testing body, not himself engaged` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- Neither engaged nor employed: no duty under (e).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(e) — an engaged or employed expert shall report each auxiliary test and give his opinion on its results` `an expert neither engaged under a tender nor employed` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)

§§ `s 34(f) -- working rules`

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(f) — a tester shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a tester` DOES `act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` AT 1
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(f) — a tester shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 34(f) — an expert shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `an expert` DOES `act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` AT 1
-- EXPECT: STANDING
#TRACE `s 34(f) — an expert shall act in accordance with the working rules the senior inspector directs` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 500)

-- s.34(f) with s.36(d) (src:287, 303): both let an official direct how testers and experts work, and the Law does
-- not say which prevails if they conflict: a named refusal, never a default.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 34(f), s 36(d) — the party whose rule governs when the instrument of authorisation and the senior inspector's working rules conflict`
